A||N||2||SloPonti||Replacing Vacuum hoses||||5||
Z||000000||SloPonti||11-30-1999||06:22 PM||||I am replacing my vacuum hoses! does anyone know what sizes i need to replace all the vacuum hoses on my 84 4 cylinder coupe! <BR>Thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||5
Z||000001||RFMike||12-02-1999||11:39 PM||||There are a variety of sizes to match, and you must also match wall strength.  If the wall isn't strong enough to resist the vacuum, it can collapse and restrict.<BR>When I have replaced vac hoses, I've taken the old one off and gone to a good hardware store (Fleet Farm- the mall for men) and matched it.<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||12-03-1999||09:48 AM||||There are a couple of vacuum lines that are preformed hard plastic that you need to get from the dealer (EGR and MAP, if memory serves).  If they're cracked, you can't fix 'em with silicone or anything like that.  Most of my other lines, I replaced with nice thick hose from the hardware store.<P>It's worth the effort.  When I replaced the vacuum lines on my 88 Coupe, my hesitation between 4000-5000 rpm disappeared.  98 hp, yessirree!!!||||reg||1
